uage models. Nvidia not only offers AI GPUs, but also a software platform, Cuda, used for AI model development and training. Nvidia is also expanding its data center networking solutions, helping to tie GPUs together to handle complex workloads.","subclass":"stock","tradable":true,"status":"active","instrument_status":"enabled","fractionable":true,"has_tokenized":true,"tokenized_symbol":"NVDAx","overnight_trading_support":"enabled","price":"226.25","volume":"69813043.312466","change":"-3.1","change_pct":"-1.351646","turnover":"15815224727.492819","high_52_week":"243.37","low_52_week":"164.27","shares":"24147000000","market_cap":"5463258750000","dividend_freq":"4","category":"Technology","industry":"Semiconductors","ipo_date":916963200,"vendor_attributes":["has_options","fractional_extended_hours_enabled"],"exchange":"NASDAQ"},{"rank":2,"symbol":"AAPL","name":"Apple Inc. Common Stock","short_name":"Apple","description":"Apple is among the largest companies in the world, with a broad portfolio of hardware and software products targeted at consumers and businesses. Apple's iPhone accounts for the majority of the firm's sales, and Apple's other products, such as the Mac, iPad, and Watch, are designed around the iPhone as the focal point of an expansive software ecosystem. Apple has progressively worked to add new applications, such as streaming video, subscription bundles, and augmented reality. The firm designs its own software and semiconductors and works with subcontractors such as Foxconn and TSMC to build its products and chips. Slightly less than half of Apple's sales come directly through its flagship stores, with the majority coming indirectly through partnerships and distribution.","subclass":"stock","tradable":true,"status":"active","instrument_status":"enabled","fractionable":true,"has_tokenized":true,"tokenized_symbol":"AAPLx","overnight_trading_support":"enabled","price":"340.9","volume":"25783906.95887","change":"4.23","change_pct":"1.256423","turnover":"8782514930.969276","high_52_week":"345.34","low_52_week":"243.42","shares":"14594180000","market_cap":"4975155962000","dividend_freq":"4","category":"Technology","industry":"Consumer Electronics","ipo_date":345427200,"vendor_attributes":["has_options","fractional_extended_hours_enabled"],"exchange":"NASDAQ"},{"rank":3,"symbol":"GOOGL","name":"Alphabet Inc. Class A Common Stock","short_name":"Alphabet (Class A)","description":"Alphabet is a holding company that wholly owns internet giant Google. The California-based company derives slightly less than 90% of its revenue from Google services, the vast majority of which is advertising sales. Alongside online ads, Google services houses sales stemming from Google's subscription services (YouTube TV and YouTube Music, among others), platforms (sales and in-app purchases on Play Store), and devices (Chromebooks, Pixel smartphones, and smart home products such as Chromecast). Google's cloud computing platform accounts for roughly 10% of Alphabet's revenue. The firm's investments in up-and-coming technologies such as self-driving cars (Waymo), health (Verily), and internet access (Google Fiber) make up the rest.","subclass":"stock","tradable":true,"status":"active","instrument_status":"enabled","fractionable":true,"has_tokenized":true,"tokenized_symbol":"GOOGLx","overnight_trading_support":"enabled","price":"352.78","volume":"18028036.02824","change":"1.1","change_pct":"0.312784","turnover":"6366582113.461709","high_52_week":"408.61","low_52_week":"239.71","shares":"12229934831","market_cap":"4314476409680","dividend_freq":"4","category":"Communication Services","industry":"Internet Content & Information","ipo_date":1092873600,"vendor_attributes":["has_options","fractional_extended_hours_enabled"],"exchange":"NASDAQ"}],"count":17048,"count_tradable":13203,"total_results":13203},"dataUpdateCount":1,"dataUpdatedAt":1791836533029,"error":null,"errorUpdateCount":0,"errorUpdatedAt":0,"fetchFailureCount":0,"fetchFailureReason":null